## Why This Is Asked
This question tests understanding of streaming cardinality estimation under memory constraints—a fundamental skill for building analytics pipelines at scale.

## Key Concepts
- **HyperLogLog**: Uses probabilistic counting to estimate cardinalities with sub-linear memory
- **Register updates**: Hash to determine bucket, count leading zeros, store maximum run length
- **Merge behavior**: Element-wise maximum of registers enables lossless parallel merging
- **Error bounds**: Relative standard error ≈ 1.04/√m; memory scales as O(m)

## Code Example
```javascript
class HyperLogLog {
  constructor(m = 128) {
    this.m = m;
    this.registers = new Uint8Array(m);
  }

  _hash(id) {
    let h = xmur3(id.toString());
    return splitmix64(h());
  }

  add(id) {
    const hash = this._hash(id);
    const idx = hash & (this.m - 1);
    const remaining = hash >>> Math.log2(this.m);
    const leadingZeros = Math.clz32(remaining) - (32 - Math.log2(this.m) - 1);
    this.registers[idx] = Math.max(this.registers[idx], leadingZeros + 1);
  }

  estimate() {
    const alpha = 0.7213 / (1 + 1.079 / this.m);
    const sum = this.registers.reduce((acc, val) => acc + Math.pow(2, -val), 0);
    return alpha * this.m * this.m / sum;
  }

  merge(other) {
    for (let i = 0; i < this.m; i++) {
      this.registers[i] = Math.max(this.registers[i], other.registers[i]);
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical amortized analysis under streaming appends with cache considerations. It evaluates understanding of how to design data structures that balance update frequency, query latency, and memory access patterns.

## Key Concepts
- **Sliding windows**: Maintaining a fixed-size view over streaming data
- **Circular buffers**: O(1) rotation without shifting elements
- **Amortized analysis**: Batched updates spread costs over time
- **Cache-friendly layout**: Sequential memory access patterns for spatial locality

## Code Example
```javascript
class StreamingAnalyticsStore {
  constructor(W, kQueries, mKeys) {
    this.W = W;
    this.blocks = [];
    this.head = 0;
    this.size = 0;
    this.windowSum = 0;
    this.queryRanges = kQueries.map(([start, end]) => ({ start, end }));
    this.keySet = new Set(mKeys);
  }

  appendBatch(newBlocks) {
    for (const block of newBlocks) {
      if (this.size === this.W) {
        this.windowSum -= this.blocks[this.head];
      }
      this.blocks[this.head] = block;
      this.windowSum += block;
      this.head = (this.head + 1) % this.W;
      this.size = Math.min(this.size + 1, this.W);
    }
  }

  rangeSum(queryIndex) {
    const { start, end } = this.queryRanges[queryIndex];
    const windowSize = this.size;
    const startIdx = (this.head - end + this.W) % this.W;
    const endIdx = (this.head - start - 1 + this.W) % this.W;
    let sum = 0;
    let i = startIdx;
    while (i !== (endIdx + 1) % this.W) {
      sum += this.blocks[i];
      i = (i + 1) % this.W;
    }
    return sum;
  }

  hasKey(key) {
    return this.keySet.has(key);
  }
}
```

